
First, we need to figure out the correct steps to take as an entire civilization and ecosystem.

Lately, I've been wondering whether many of us have become disconnected from our own minds and bodies. I don't know exactly what that means yet, but it's something I've been thinking about a lot.

I also believe that if people were completely honest about what they've seen, heard, felt, and experienced, we might be better able to understand what's happening around us and figure out how to approach it together.

One observation I've made is that something as simple as gently holding onto a loved one while staying completely relaxed and paying close attention can reveal things that we normally overlook. I'm not claiming to know exactly what it means, only that it has repeatedly made me question whether we need to look at ourselves and our bodies differently.

Over time, I've noticed what feels like a vibration in every person I've intentionally tried this with. 

What surprised me most was that they usually couldn't feel it themselves. Even when I was still holding onto them and discussing it, they often had no awareness of what I was experiencing.

This first caught my attention when my grandmother was still alive. Before she passed away, I would give her massages and spend time paying attention to how her body was functioning. At first, I thought what I was noticing might be connected to age or dementia. However, according to the information available to us, her body was actually in very good condition for someone in her nineties.

Personally, I never felt that the symptoms I observed were caused entirely by dementia. To me, they often appeared more closely connected to emotional states. I believe that other issues and unseen environmental influences may have also added to the list of symptoms. I understand that not everyone will agree with that conclusion, but it is something I strongly believe based on my own experiences.

At one point, I managed to recreate a similar sensation within my own body. By lying down, completely relaxing, and focusing my attention inward, I began noticing the same type of vibration that I had observed in others.

I did this by intentionally relaxing and concentrating on receiving information from my body rather than trying to control it. After maintaining that focus for a period of time, I was able to even increase the clarity of the vibration of both legs and increase the vibrations with negative feedback. The moment that I releasedcontrol, effort, negative feedback, and concentration is when my legs went back to the restless state.

I don't claim to have all the answers, and I'm not telling anyone what to believe. I'm simply sharing my observations in the hope that others might pay closer attention to their own experiences and share what they discover. While hopefully creating a chance to save our planet.
